WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:07.244
Scoping and reading the assessment supports
two controls in NIST special publication

3
00:00:07.244 --> 00:00:10.345
eight hundred fifty-three,
revision five: C A two,

4
00:00:10.345 --> 00:00:14.163
control assessments, and C A
seven, continuous monitoring.

5
00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:18.649
The approved decision record evidences
planning the assessment and its scope.

6
00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:20.925
Each pillar owner's dated reading notes

7
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:23.613
evidence that the owners
reviewed the results.

8
00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:28.688
And the calendar entry, with its owner,
evidences the frequency of assessment.

9
00:00:28.688 --> 00:00:32.913
Each row also names a fed-ramp
twenty X key security indicator.

10
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:36.163
Those indicators are written
for cloud service providers.

11
00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:41.013
The agency lines its own evidence up with
them; it doesn't report them itself.

12
00:00:41.013 --> 00:00:44.850
The evidence supports the
controls, and the assessor decides.

13
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.251
So the evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module is the

14
00:00:48.251 --> 00:00:52.420
approved decision record and each
owner's dated reading notes.
